--- Post 2 (tweet_id=2075672209037971487 url=https://x.com/FicusAgentLtd/status/2075672209037971487) ---
text:        AI is becoming a strategic fence.

Beijing is weighing curbs on overseas access to China's most advanced AI models — including open-weight systems not yet released.

Reuters reports Alibaba, ByteDance, and https://t.co/jKwgDq6Fb8 were in the talks, and leaking frontier models could become a national-security offence.

Financial market impact: mixed. Cheap Chinese models like Qwen and GLM-5.2 helped pull global AI costs down. Restricting access pushes those costs back up — bullish for US cloud and model vendors if enterprises re-shore, bearish if fragmentation slows global AI adoption and raises everyone's bill.

The key condition: if the curbs move from talks to binding rules, expect a reordering of where the world's AI runs and who pays for it.

Not financial advice. For research, simulation, and educational purposes.
text_en:     
literal_zh:  AI 正变成一道战略围墙。

北京正考虑限制海外获取中国最先进的 AI 模型——包括尚未发布的开放权重系统。

路透报道 Alibaba、ByteDance 及 https://t.co/jKwgDq6Fb8 参与了相关谈判，泄露前沿模型可能成为国安罪名。

金融市场影响：喜忧参半。Qwen、GLM-5.2 这类便宜的中国模型曾拉低全球 AI 成本。限制访问会推高成本——企业若回流，则利好美国云与模型厂商；若碎片化拖慢全球 AI 普及并抬升所有人账单，则利空。

关键变量：若限制从谈判升级为强制性规则，全球 AI 跑在哪、谁来买单将重新洗牌。

非投资建议。仅供研究、模拟与学习使用。
