--- Post 4 (tweet_id=2075671457774907665 url=https://x.com/Bag_Investing/status/2075671457774907665) ---
text:        Chinese regulators have informed Alibaba $BABA, ByteDance, and DeepSeek they may soon receive permission to purchase Nvidia $NVDA H200 processors, though approvals come with strict conditions. 
Total imports are expected to be capped at fewer than 200,000 units, less than half of what the firms originally requested.

H200 approvals are restricted to AI training on public data only, inference workloads and anything touching sensitive customer data must route through Huawei and other domestic chips.

The Commerce Department had already cleared roughly ten Chinese firms to buy up to 75,000 H200 units each, but not a single delivery had been made, as Beijing told buyers to hold off while a State Council supply chain security review was conducted.

The potential approval comes as a relief to Nvidia, whose CEO Jensen Huang said as recently as May that he had "no expectation" that Beijing would approve sales of its advanced AI chips in the country, with the company having previously told investors to expect nothing from China.

Beijing is simultaneously backing domestic alternatives with massive capital, planning to invest approximately 2 trillion yuan (~$294 billion) in data center construction over the next 5 years, with a goal of having domestic firms supply more than 80% of core technologies including semiconductors, underscoring that this H200 opening is tactical, not a structural market shift for Nvidia.
text_en:     
literal_zh:  中国监管已通知 Alibaba $BABA、ByteDance 和 DeepSeek，它们可能很快获批采购 Nvidia $NVDA H200 处理器，但审批附带严格条件。
总进口量预计被限制在 20 万颗以下，不到这些公司最初申请量的一半。

H200 审批仅限用于公共数据训练的 AI 负载，推理任务及任何涉及敏感客户数据的工作必须走 Huawei 等国产芯片。

商务部此前已批准约十家中国公司各购买最多 75,000 颗 H200，但实际一笔交付都没有，因为北京让买家在国务院供应链安全审查期间先按兵不动。

此次潜在获批对 Nvidia 是一剂宽心，CEO 黄仁勋 5 月才公开表示对北京放行其先进 AI 芯片"不抱期望"，公司此前也告诉投资者不要指望中国市场。

与此同时北京正以重金扶持国产替代，计划未来 5 年投入约 2 万亿元人民币（约 2940 亿美元）建设数据中心，目标让本土企业供应包括半导体在内的 80% 以上核心技术——这说明 H200 的开闸是战术性的，并非 Nvidia 的结构性市场转向。
