--- Post 5 (tweet_id=2075671342829961442 url=https://x.com/EugenioFierro3/status/2075671342829961442) ---
text:        Meta opens its new AI model's API to developers

Meta says its new Muse Spark 1.1 model is ready to compete on coding and agentic tasks, and for the first time developers can plug it in through a brand new paid API.

🧠 After relaunching its in-house AI ambitions with the first Muse Spark model back in April, Meta is now rolling out Muse Spark 1.1, which the company calls a step-change from the first generation. Meta says it can detect and fix complex bugs, handle end-to-end agentic workflows across multiple apps including multi-agent systems, and natively understand images, video and documents.

💰 The bigger news, though, is business, not just tech. For the first time, Meta is putting a price tag on one of its own frontier models through the new Meta Model API, now in public preview for US developers, with $20 in free credits for every new account. That's a real shift for a company that built its AI reputation on giving away open weight Llama models.

📸 This launch lands just days after Muse Image, Meta's image generation model, drew criticism for pulling other users' Instagram content into its outputs. Both releases are part of Meta's push to justify the billions it has poured into catching up with OpenAI, Google and Anthropic, following high-profile hires and an internal reorg over the past year.

📱 Muse Spark 1.1 is already live in Thinking mode inside the Meta AI app and website, and it's likely to eventually power the chatbots inside Instagram and WhatsApp, plus Meta's smart glasses, the same path the first Muse Spark took.

Why it matters: if Meta can genuinely deliver a model that's competitive on coding and automation at an aggressive price compared to OpenAI and Anthropic, that changes the calculation for anyone picking a provider to build production AI agents on. This isn't just about downloading open weights anymore, it's about choosing managed infrastructure to build on, with everything that means for cost and vendor lock-in.

What strikes me most isn't the spec sheet, it's the shift in posture. Going from "here are the weights, build whatever you want" to "pay us to use our model" tells me Meta finally believes it has something good enough to sell, not just give away to grow an ecosystem. Whether developers trust a closed Meta model as much as they trust OpenAI or Anthropic today is the real question this launch raises.

📱 Want AI updates on WhatsApp? DM me "AI" and I'll send you access.
🔔 Follow me for the last AI updates!

#AInews #Meta #MuseSpark #AICoding #TechNews
text_en:     
literal_zh:  Meta 向开发者开放新 AI 模型 API

Meta 表示新 Muse Spark 1.1 模型已准备好在编程和 Agent 任务上竞争，开发者首次可通过全新付费 API 接入。

🧠 在 4 月用初代 Muse Spark 重启自研 AI 战略后，Meta 正在推出 Muse Spark 1.1，公司称之为代际跃迁。Meta 称其能检测并修复复杂 bug，跨多个 App 跑端到端 Agent 工作流（包含多 Agent 系统），并原生理解图像、视频与文档。

💰 但更大的新闻在商业层面，不只是技术。Meta 首次通过全新 Meta Model API 给自家前沿模型明码标价，现已对美国开发者公测预览，新账号送 $20 免费额度。对一家靠送 Llama 开放权重打江山 AI 口碑的公司来说，这是个真转变。

📸 这次发布落地前几天，Muse Image——Meta 的图像生成模型——刚因把其他用户的 Instagram 内容混进输出而挨骂。两项发布都服务于 Meta 证明自己烧了几十亿追 OpenAI、Google、Anthropic 是合理的，过去一年的重磅招聘与内部重组都为此铺垫。

📱 Muse Spark 1.1 已在 Meta AI App 和网站内的 Thinking 模式上线，并很可能最终接入 Instagram、WhatsApp 内的聊天机器人，以及 Meta 智能眼镜——和初代 Muse Spark 的路径一致。

为何重要：如果 Meta 真能在编程与自动化任务上以激进价格拿出与 OpenAI、Anthropic 抗衡的模型，那就改变了任何人在挑选生产级 AI Agent 供应商时的算式。这已不只是下载开放权重的事，而是选择在哪家托管基础设施上盖楼，连带着成本与供应商锁定问题。

最让我在意的不是参数表，而是姿态的转变。从"权重给你，爱怎么玩怎么玩"到"付钱用我们的模型"，这告诉我 Meta 终于相信自己手里这东西好到能卖，而不是只靠白送去养生态。开发者能否像信任 OpenAI、Anthropic 那样信任一个闭源的 Meta 模型，才是这次发布真正抛出的问题。

